comments[18]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T18:46:41.257Z",codex-sol,"Main fc7e396 still classifies only type, title and resolution signals; no contract migration projection exists. Implement a shared metadata.contract_change projection for Markdown, JSON and audit, retaining unchanged output for undeclared items. Add real SDK non-git tracker regressions before implementation; PR 324 is excluded."
  "2026-11-06T18:50:33.381Z",codex-sol,"Baseline reproduction at fc7e396: both focused tests fail behaviorally. SDK-created declarations render under Fixed and Security with no migration line; audit reports Fixed and no migration gap. The producer uses a native object schema field and the SDK contractChange option because project fields reject --field (expected declared-flag policy). Shared projection now covers Markdown, JSON, grouping, breaking deduplication and milestone capture."
  "2026-11-06T18:53:22.487Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral revert proof in a disposable copy: restored only classifyItem, groupByField, formatItem, toDocumentItem, auditChangelogClaims and renderItem from origin/main; rebuilt dist successfully; all 6 contract-change tests failed (0 passed, 6 failed). The package worktree stayed fixed. Focused restored implementation passed 6/6; audit and milestone compatibility checks passed 39/39. Run final npm and Bun release checks at unchanged thresholds after linked test execution and changelog regeneration."
  "2026-11-06T19:02:36.609Z",codex-sol,"Refinement preserves underlying evidence and semver classification independently of the Changed presentation group. Targeted contract and claim-audit checks pass 19/19; typecheck, test typecheck and docstring checks pass. Fresh disposable main-function revert (groupByCategory, groupByField, formatItem, toDocumentItem, auditChangelogClaims, renderItem) builds and fails all 6 regressions. Independently reverting only the classification refinement to the first PR head builds and fails the evidence/semver regression (1/1 failed). An exploratory local full gate was stopped without a verdict before this refinement; restart final gates serially. PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/328; CodeRabbit is queued."
  "2026-11-06T19:29:57.601Z",codex-sol,"Implementation and local verification complete: targeted contract-change, claim-audit and milestone suite passes 43/43, zero failures/skips/cancellations. Typecheck, test typecheck, docstring/lint gate (266 declarations across 41 files) and diff whitespace checks pass. All 6 regressions fail after a main-function behavioral revert and successful rebuild; independent classification-refinement revert fails its evidence/semver regression. Published CLI 2026.11.5 inspection found no explicit contract-change field signature in 2989 declarations; the consumer metadata format is documented and no dependency pin changed. Task-specific local gates are targeted tests/lint/typecheck; exploratory full checks were stopped without a complete verdict, leaving the unchanged full gate to CI. PR 328: CodeRabbit queue pending; current CI and CodeQL runs are queued. Record final-head CI/review results in the PR after this tracker handoff; no merge or release. PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/328"
  "2026-11-06T21:11:07.644Z",codex-sol,"Resumed PR 328 after CI completion: current head f5f982c has no unresolved review threads and no completed CodeRabbit review. CI lifecycle and downstream test job are marked failed; inspect exact failed steps and logs before changing code. Preserve the completed implementation and existing revert proofs. The worktree is clean and synced with its branch."
  "2026-11-06T21:12:38.662Z",codex-sol,"CI diagnosis: run 42280506150 was canceled by the repository owner before either lifecycle or test received a runner. Both jobs have empty step lists; the lifecycle annotation records owner cancellation. There is no executed test assertion or workflow step failure to repair. Preserve source and gates unchanged; the existing 43-test acceptance set and behavioral revert proofs remain applicable. A tracker-only handoff push will trigger fresh exact-head CI and requeue the required review. Prior CI receipt: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/42280506150 . Current review snapshot: zero unresolved threads, zero completed CodeRabbit reviews."
  "2026-11-06T23:41:48.234Z",codex-agent,"Review round: fetched all three unresolved threads including every comment; latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. All three are valid. Plan: exercise active-extension runUpdate, retain neutral closure precedence across Markdown/JSON/summary grouping, isolate contract field code spans with complete equal-length backtick matching, and prove regressions through behavioral reverts in a disposable copy. Branch already contains current origin/main."
  "2026-11-06T23:45:27.172Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: node scripts/prove-contract-changes-revert.ts passed 9 isolated fixed-pass / behavioral-revert-fail / restored-pass cases. PRRT_kwDOSfkApc60txTs: removing only the contract_change registration from activate (and rebuilding copied dist) makes the real runUpdate test fail with extension_item_field_unknown. PRRT_kwDOSfkApc60txTy: removing the neutral-closure guard fails the all-output test; separate reverts of JSON title, summary title, category grouping and field grouping also fail. PRRT_kwDOSfkApc60txT3: reverting field isolation, equal complete backtick matching or unmatched-run recovery independently fails the Markdown-parser test. All reverts ran in a disposable copy and restored passing behavior. Whole-PR self-review found the same closure bypass in category grouping, JSON and summary output and fixed them with the shared presentation guard. Focused contract suite: 9 passed, 0 failed/skipped. No findings refused."
  "2026-11-07T00:19:37.089Z",codex-agent,"Gate progress: targeted node --test --test-concurrency=2 suite passed 562/562 across contract-changes, closure-evidence, closure-status-roles, claim-audit, entry-from, enhancements, generator-coverage, generator, extension, milestones, shipped-docs, identity-audit, package-metadata and verify-package. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test and npm run docstring pass (266 declarations, 42 files); no separate lint script is configured. npm run audit:prod, npm run pack:dry-run and npm run pack:scan pass (111 files, zero package failures). npm run changelog:check, npm run verify:release-changelog-date and npm run verify:release-publish-attestation pass. bun test/bun-milestones-smoke.ts passes CLI and SDK 2/2 without git. Isolated tracker health passes the CI policy with only its exact existing 32-event legacy provenance warning. npm run release:check remains active in the existing 500-lifecycle model after over 30 minutes; full-suite certification is still pending, and the paired npm/Bun full gates may exceed the local time budget. No thresholds changed."
  "2026-11-07T00:23:45.025Z",codex-agent,"Final local full-gate disposition: npm run release:check was stopped deliberately after about 35 minutes while its existing 500-lifecycle model was still active; it produced no full-suite verdict and no observed assertion failure. The paired npm/Bun full runs are not expected to fit within about one hour on this host, so bun run release:check was not started. Full release certification, including unchanged 100% line/branch/function coverage thresholds, is deferred to CI. All required targeted and standalone gates previously recorded passed; direct Bun CLI/SDK smoke passed 2/2. No validation processes were left running. Review threads were neither replied to nor resolved; no merge or release. GitHub GraphQL quota was exhausted only after the complete initial thread/review fetch; REST remains usable for final PR and CI receipts. Ready for orchestrator verification after the code, generated dist and append-only pm evidence are pushed."
  "2026-11-07T02:13:39.648Z",codex-agent,"Resumed review round after clean status and existing receipts check. Fresh remote main was one commit ahead; merge it before fixes. Two unresolved findings are valid: PRRT_kwDOSfkApc60w0W6 (null direct contract metadata shadows valid nested metadata) and PRRT_kwDOSfkApc60vzXu (contract summary title bypasses single-line normalization). General rules: nullish compatibility projections must fall back without discarding auditable standalone malformed values; line-oriented output normalizes every projected title through the same presentation policy. Search the whole package and exercise SDK, CLI, JSON/TOON, snapshots and packed Node/Bun consumers in synthetic non-git fixtures. Preserve previous regression tests and prove only new behavioral reverts in disposable copies."
  "2026-11-07T02:22:30.524Z",codex-agent,"Class search completed across src, scripts, tests and public CLI/SDK projections. readContractChange is the sole contract source-precedence reader; all consumers already share it. Fix nullish fallback while preserving standalone null and malformed non-null direct values, including undefined-direct/nested-null history. getStringField already validates before metadata fallback; additive breaking flags and audience declarations have distinct existing contracts and are unchanged. Route summary and JSON titles through resolveEntryTitle, keep neutral closure first and explicit declaration titles ahead of close_reason, and normalize the final summary line to bound caller-supplied heading/version/category/title/id. Baseline: all 3 new adversarial tests failed. Fixed: 13/13 contract tests passed, including 90 precedence pairs through JSON/TOON round trips, 100 seeded titles across 8 grouping/entry-source combinations, and real offline npm-packed Node/Bun SDK/CLI/host consumers using synthetic non-git trackers. Prior neutral-JSON assertions were strengthened rather than weakened."
  "2026-11-07T02:23:38.778Z",codex-agent,"Revert proof: node scripts/prove-contract-changes-revert.ts passed all 14 fixed-pass / behavioral-revert-fail / restored-pass cases in a disposable copy. Five new independent reverts cover PRRT_kwDOSfkApc60w0W6 (restore undefined-only precedence), PRRT_kwDOSfkApc60vzXu (restore raw summary titles), the matching raw JSON-title bypass, removal of shared declared-title/entry-source policy, and removal of final one-line formatting. Each reverted behavior fails its adversarial property test with ERR_ASSERTION and passes again after restoration. The previous nine revert cases remain passing after the shared title refactor and main merge; neutral JSON now also asserts absence of contract metadata. No existing test was deleted or weakened. Full release gates will be attempted serially with at most two workers and a combined local time budget, preserving all thresholds."
  "2026-11-07T02:58:27.327Z",codex-agent,"Current-head gate progress: the broader 16-file targeted suite passed 576/576, zero failures/skips/cancellations, including main ordering regressions. Typecheck, test typecheck and docstrings pass (266 declarations across 42 scanned files). Production audit found zero vulnerabilities; package allowlist and content scans each checked 111 files with zero failures. Changelog generation/link checking and release date/publication-attestation checks pass. The serial npm full release gate is still active in the existing 500-lifecycle model, with zero reported test failures so far and no full-suite verdict. Bun full release certification waits behind npm within the combined one-hour local budget. Existing full thresholds are unchanged; completed targeted evidence and all 14 revert proofs are retained."
  "2026-11-07T03:04:31.117Z",codex-agent,"Full npm release gate passed on the candidate source and rebuilt dist: npm run release:check completed in 2079 seconds; 1025/1025 tests passed, zero failures/skips/cancellations. Coverage presence reconciled all 29 required source files with 100% lines, branches and functions at unchanged thresholds. Docstrings, zero-vulnerability production audit, both 111-file package checks, changelog/link checks, release-date and publication-attestation checks passed within the full gate. Bun full release gate is running serially with the remainder of the combined one-hour local budget. Local evidence describes the candidate worktree; fresh CI on the eventual pushed head remains a separate receipt."
  "2026-11-07T03:29:00.682Z",codex-agent,"Final gate disposition: npm run release:check passed 1025/1025 with zero failures/skips and 100% lines/branches/functions across all 29 required source files, in 2079 seconds. bun run release:check ran serially for 1520 seconds and was stopped by the combined one-hour local budget while the existing 500-lifecycle model remained active; no full Bun verdict or reported test failure was obtained. Full Bun certification remains for CI; actual packed Bun SDK/CLI/host acceptance already passed within the 13-test focused and 576-test targeted runs. All 14 behavioral revert proofs passed. Validated source/test/docs/dist blob hashes remain unchanged, and no owned validation processes remain. Both open findings are fixed across their classes; no findings were refused. Latest complete thread read still has the same two threads, left unanswered/unresolved as instructed. Release the claim and keep the item in progress for orchestrator verification; no PR merge or release."
  "2026-11-07T13:43:47.453Z",codex-agent,"Resumed auto review round 2 after checking the clean worktree and prior pm receipts. Both current threads are valid and share one class: audit diagnostics must describe only contract assertions actually published, using the same eligibility policy as rendering. PRRT_kwDOSfkApc60xoWw and PRRT_kwDOSfkApc60xqLq flag raw contract metadata audited even when neutral Closed rendering suppresses it. Merge current main first, preserving its publication and dependency changes. Reuse one shared declaration-presentation helper across Markdown/JSON/summary/audit, retain ordinary evidence gaps, search the full package for duplicate decisions, and add adversarial/property plus packed Node/Bun non-git acceptance and isolated behavioral revert proofs. Do not repeat completed previous-round work or alter any existing threshold."
